#: ../../source/docs/channel-output-functions.rst:9
#: 1ee8ecc5076b4e7ca1b5f1d8b9eb46d4
msgid "All servo outputs may be mapped to any function supported by ArduPilot. The default settings are for the first 4 channels to be Aileron, Elevator, Throttle and Rudder (commonly known as AETR), but you can re-assign them as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/channel-output-functions.rst:14
#: 4b8d1c686e974e0d898b2cfcc73f1e6e
msgid "This page describes how to configure these output channels and what each of the available functions is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/channel-output-functions.rst:18
#: 2bfb07c25382442fa14d0f8de5404030
msgid "The SERVOn_FUNCTION parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/channel-output-functions.rst:20
#: 1d4e928252fe40c59936016db8bcae36
msgid "In the advanced parameter view of your GCS you will find that each SERVO output channel has a SERVOn_FUNCTION parameter. For example, :ref:`SERVO5_FUNCTION<SERVO5_FUNCTION>` controls the output function of channel 5, :ref:`SERVO6_FUNCTION<SERVO6_FUNCTION>` controls the output function of channel 6 and so on."
msgstr ""

